        "denialFound": "None found, and not asked. The claim alleges no wrongdoing, so no response is needed. The figures are self-reported by the Delhi Prisons Department to NCRB (\"As per data provided by States/UTs\").",
        "innocentReading": "Delhi's prisons (Tihar, Rohini and Mandoli) serve a metropolitan court system with a very high undertrial share: 88.8% against 73.5% nationally (PSI 2023 Table 2.2). Capacity has not grown with remand inflow. Prisons are run by GNCTD, while Delhi Police reports to the MHA, so the occupancy figure does not attribute blame to either authority. Tihar has run above 150% for well over a decade under governments of different parties. On symmetry, the same lens puts BJP-run Maharashtra and MP next in line. No party-political reading follows.",
        "reason": "Every number checks against PSI 2023 Table 1.4: 14 jails, capacity 9,346, inmates 19,362, 207.2%, national 120.7%. The ranking among states/UTs with 2 or more central jails holds; the runner-up is Maharashtra at 175.4%. The claim implies no impropriety, and the source URL is live. The one flaw is in the text field: \"not policing\" overstates the innocent reading. The record's own innocentReading says \"as much as of policing\", and the evidence does not exclude policing (arrest and remand volume). Analytic is the right tier for a rank built from a primary table. The underlying figures are themselves documented.",
        "corrections": [
          "text: change \"Innocent reading: undertrial load and court throughput, not policing\" to \"Innocent reading: undertrial load (88.8% of Delhi inmates vs 73.5% national, PSI Table 2.2), capacity additions and court throughput, as much as policing\". This aligns it with the record's innocentReading field. d: optionally add \"all-jail occupancy 200.2% (Table 1.3), also highest of any state/UT\" so the ranking does not depend on the ≥2-central-jail cutoff. srcs label: add Table 2.2 if the undertrial share is cited. No change to tier, amounts, date or nodes."
        ],
