        "sourceCheck": "confirmed",
        "denialFound": "None found, and none was sought. The claim imputes no conduct to any party, so no response is owed. The figures are the government's own budget numbers as transcribed by PRS.",
        "innocentReading": "Pensions are deferred pay owed under service contracts. Their share rose because of policy choices about people: OROP (2015) and the 7th CPC (2016). It does not show waste. PRS also notes that the 2025-26 pension line is inflated by a one-off Rs 8,000 crore recovery from a deposit account. One error in the record's innocentReading: it says \"about 26.8 lakh pensioners\", but ORF gives 32,94,181 pensioners as of 1 April 2021 (26,79,645 military veterans or dependents plus 6,14,536 defence civilians). The pension line covers both groups.",
        "reason": "Every number checks out against the sources, which I opened and quoted. In the PRS PDF, Table 2 has Pension 1,60,795, Salaries 1,77,923 and Total 6,81,210 for 2025-26 BE. The text says \"In 2025-26, 24% of the total defence budget is estimated to be spent on pension\" and \"Salaries and pension account for 50% of the estimated spending on defence in 2025-26.\" The ORF brief says \"79 percent of the MoD's total revenue expenditure\" for 2022-23, and gives pension growth of 163% against 107% for MoD overall between 2013-14 and 2022-23. My arithmetic: 23.6% and 49.7%. The claim does not combine facts to imply wrongdoing, names no individual and contains no operational detail. Analytic is a conservative tier. Because both outlets state these exact percentages themselves, 'reported' would also be defensible. The fixes needed are wording only: say BE, say \"MoD total allocation\", and correct the pensioner count.",
        "corrections": [
          "1. text/lab: replace \"the 2025-26 defence demand\" with \"the MoD's total 2025-26 BE allocation (Rs 6,81,210 crore, all demands)\". 2. text/d: change \"79% of revenue expenditure 2022-23\" to \"79% of MoD revenue expenditure, 2022-23 BE (ORF, Aug 2023)\". 3. d: add PRS's caveats that \"salaries\" includes civilians, R&D and civil estimates but leaves out Rashtriya Rifles, NCC and the Agnipath cadre, and that the 2025-26 pension line includes a Rs 8,000 crore deposit-account recovery. 4. innocentReading: change \"about 26.8 lakh pensioners\" to \"about 32.9 lakh pensioners (26.8 lakh military veterans or dependents plus 6.1 lakh defence civilians, as of 1 Apr 2021, per ORF)\". 5. Optional: the tier could be raised to 'reported' with note 'reported: PRS transcription of Union Budget 2025-26', because the percentages are stated verbatim by PRS and ORF, not computed by us. Keeping 'analytic' is acceptable."
        ],
