        "denialFound": "This record is itself the government's response. Contrary material exists. (a) The SC order of 2019-04-10 (https://indiankanoon.org/doc/126750916/) rejected the privilege argument, saying s.123 covers \"unpublished public records\", while \"the three documents have been published in different editions of 'The Hindu'\". (b) The CAG report of February 2019 is reported to have found the IGA about 2.86% cheaper, not 9–20%. literature.json line ~1010 records this as not opened because cag.gov.in was unreachable. (c) Congress (Surjewala, Rahul Gandhi) disputes the comparison (Wikipedia).",
