        "reason": "The headline survives: the privilege claim was rejected by the SC, and a 9–20% saving was claimed. The SC order confirms the privilege part verbatim, and Wikipedia confirms the 9%/20% figures. But the `d` field puts figures in the mouth of \"the then Defence Minister\" when the source gives them to M.J. Akbar and Arun Jaitley. It also uses ₹526 crore where that chain started at ₹538 crore. And the subject is MoD for statements made by other ministers and the AG. Putting a statement in the mouth of an office-holder who did not make it fails the identity test. The 2019-03 date and the `contra` target also fit only the privilege part. Treat the record as refuted until it is corrected; once corrected it stands at `reported`.",
