        "denialFound": "The exculpatory record is in the cited source itself. Delhi HC, 4 February 2004 (https://indiankanoon.org/doc/561739/): the ASG for CBI conceded that, as to bribe receipt by public servants, \"till date there was none\". The court held the late PM \"is entitled to be seen as innocent\". BBC, 25 April 2012 (cited on Wikipedia): Swedish investigator Sten Lindstrom said there was \"No evidence Rajiv Gandhi took bribe\". The JPC report (1988) found no evidence that the payments violated Indian law. I found no separate 2026 statement from the Hindujas or Bofors, and none appears to have been sought. Both Hinduja respondents who died (Srichand and Gopichand) are deceased.",
        "innocentReading": "Bofors paid commissions to agents. That breached its assurance to the Government of India that it used no middlemen, and the HC judgment documents those payments. But a payment to an agent is not a bribe to a public servant. In 2004 the prosecution conceded it had no evidence of receipt by officials. The 2011 and 2026 disposals reflect evidentiary failure, deaths, and a 4,522-day CBI delay rather than a finding of either guilt or innocence. The claim's wording \"recipient side never established\" already states this reading correctly.",
        "reason": "The core conjunction survives. Payments to agents are confirmed by a primary court record: the Delhi HC says CBI \"succeeded in tracing the Swiss accounts of 'Commission Agents' employed by M/s A.B. Bofors wherein illegal payments received by them from Bofors as commission were deposited\". The same judgment records the ASG's concession that there was no evidence of public servants receiving bribes. The 4 March 2011 Quattrocchi closure and the 6 August 2026 SC dismissal are reported by multiple outlets (HT, DNA, Republic, NewsX). Two errors need fixing. First, the d-field attributes the 2026 plea to CBI, but it was the private appellant Ajay K Agrawal's appeal; CBI's own appeal died in November 2018 on delay. Second, \"Swiss documents (1997)\" understates the timeline: the documents came in tranches from 1990 to 2000, and the 1997 tranche is not shown to be the one that \"establishes\" the payments. As sourced, the record rests on Wikipedia for 2011 and 2026, so it stays at reported. It becomes documented once the HT and DNA URLs (or the SC order itself) are added; the agent-payment and no-recipient elements already rest on a court order.",
