          "1) Text/framing: change \"Italian courts ended in acquittal (2018, upheld 2019)\" to \"Italian proceedings against the individual executives ended in acquittal (Milan appeal 2018-01-08, upheld by the Cassazione 2019-05-22); the two AgustaWestland companies took a 2014 Busto Arsizio plea bargain (EUR 7.5m confiscation plus administrative fines), which is not a guilt finding; consultant Haschke was acquitted on appeal in Brescia 2025-06-30\". Add sources: Il Fatto Quotidiano 2014-08-28 (https://www.ilfattoquotidiano.it/2014/08/28/finmeccanica-agustawestland-patteggia-7-milioni-e-mezzo-per-tangenti-in-india/1101205/) and the Reuters 2025-07-01 report on the Haschke acquittal. 2) Subject node: replace \"s\":\"agencies\" with the CBI node (and add a separate ED edge for the PMLA case if one is wanted). 3) d field: note the 4/5 December 2018 extradition-date ambiguity in the source. 4) Update the status line: Delhi HC 2026-04-08 rejected Michel's plea for release; SC issued notice in May 2026 on his specialty/continued-detention challenge; no Indian verdict as of 2026-10. 5) Add a contra: Tyagi's denial and his counsel's statement in court (india.com, 2016). 6) Upgrade path: open the TOI FIR report and The Hindu PE/arrest reports cited by Wikipedia. Two independent outlets would meet the contract's bar for \"documented\". 7) The Tatra control node needs a matching FIR, chargesheet and outcome record before the SPEC symmetry check can be run."
