        "denialFound": "The responses are on record but none was pulled into this record. Rafale: Defence Minister Sitharaman denied procedural wrongdoing and said CCS approval preceded the IGA (cited on the Rafale Wikipedia page). Dassault and the GoI rejected the Mediapart and PNF allegations. Bofors: Rajiv Gandhi denied in Parliament in 1987 that he or his family received money, and the Hindujas denied throughout. The claim should cite at least one response per side. None was asked by this platform.",
        "innocentReading": "Big-ticket foreign arms purchases in India regularly draw allegations, leaked files, PILs and foreign investigations. Indian courts rarely convict because of evidence held abroad, the deaths of accused, delay, and deference to the executive on defence. That a scandal and a non-scandal \"end the same way\" is a finding about Indian criminal process, not proof that the two cases are equally strong. Bofors had documented illegal commissions. Rafale, as of the record, has no documented payment to an Indian official.",
