        "denialFound": "Michel has denied wrongdoing throughout. In his bail application he called the CBI allegations \"absolutely false and baseless\" (reported, e.g. Deccan Herald https://www.deccanherald.com/india/middleman-michel-claims-he-never-2064871; The Wire https://m.thewire.in/article/law/let-me-remain-in-tihar-augustawestland-accused-christian-michel-refuses-bail). Italy's Court of Cassation (2019) upheld the acquittals in the Italian proceedings. This edge records only procedural events (extradition, bail, stage), not guilt, so the denial belongs on the c071 'alleged' edge's contra, not here. Gulf News carries no statement from Michel or his lawyer about the SC bail.",
        "innocentReading": "The edge says only that an accused was extradited, got bail from the SC and the HC after more than six years of custody, and that charges were not yet framed after seven years. That reflects slow investigation and multi-agency (CBI/ED) proceedings, not a finding of guilt or innocence. Nothing in it implies wrongdoing by any government, and it is as consistent with prosecutorial delay as with a strong case.",
        "reason": "The claim is not refuted. All four dated facts check out against the sources. The Gulf News quote confirms the SC bail of 18 Feb 2025. ANI and Business Standard (dated 4 Mar 2025) confirm the Delhi HC bail in the ED case on 4 Mar 2025, which the record wrongly described as resting on a 'search summary'. LawBeat quotes the Special CBI Judge's line that \"charges are yet to be decided\". Gulf News places the extradition arrest on 4 Dec 2018. The only variance is Wikipedia's 5 Dec 2018, explained by the late-night arrival. The edge is a conjunction of procedural facts and draws no further inference. 'Reported' is the right tier and is conservative. Each date except the 23 Dec stage has two or more independent outlets, but the charges-not-framed element rests on one outlet's report of the order, not the order itself.",
