        "denialFound": "Yes, and the record does not carry it. In 2012 Tejinder Singh publicly denied the allegation as \"absolutely false and concocted\" and filed a criminal defamation complaint against Gen V K Singh and four officers (Deccan Herald / Tribune 2012 coverage, e.g. https://www.deccanherald.com/content/238536/army-chief-names-tejinder-cbi.html and https://www.tribuneindia.com/2012/20120426/main3.htm). In his statement to the CBI he admitted the meeting but said he went to seek support for the NTRO chief's post. In 2013 the CBI was reported to be closing the preliminary enquiry for lack of evidence (Hindustan Times 1 Jul 2013 via PressReader). In the HC his counsel argued that no s.12 offence was made out. The record does carry A K Antony's 2022 testimony that the Chief gave no note or recording, which supports the defence.",
        "innocentReading": "Framing a charge needs only a prima facie case, and the HC's refusal to interfere at that stage is not a finding of guilt. The case rests on the complainant's word about a private meeting. The accused admits meeting him and gives another purpose for it, and the then Defence Minister testified that he received no documentary or audio evidence. No trial outcome was found. The accused is presumed innocent.",
        "reason": "The substance survives. Charges were framed on 2 Aug 2019 on Gen V K Singh's complaint of a Rs 14 crore offer for 1676 HMVs, and the Delhi HC (Kaurav J) held the order \"does not call for any interference\". Both secondary sources say this, and the primary judgment confirms it. The claim cannot pass as written, though. The HC decision was given on 20.07.2022, not 2022-07-22 (the press date). The accused's public denial and his defamation complaint are missing from the record. Once the judgment URL is added as a source, this is a primary court record, so `documented` is the right tier for the stage facts (charge framed, revision dismissed). The bribe offer itself stays an allegation under trial.",
