        "innocentReading": "The seven cases are the famous ones, and which cases become famous depends on who is in opposition at the time. Older cases have had longer to reach a stage. Indian corruption prosecutions of senior officials rarely end in conviction under any government. Court-martial verdicts were set aside on procedure (GCM composition) and on findings that the proceedings were 'influenced and vitiated', not as a judgment on the government. Having no FIR (Rafale, Pegasus) and having an FIR without a conviction are different outcomes, but neither proves anyone guilty or innocent.",
