        "innocentReading": "L&T has been a licensed defence prime for decades, building warships, radars and K9 guns. Adani Defence entered around 2015-18 and so far wins mainly through JVs (PLR with IWI) and development programmes (Netra Mk2 DcPP L1, which is DRDO, not a signed MoD contract). On the second-bidder rule: when the L2 bidder matches the L1 price, defence procurement rules allow the order to be split 60:40, which is ordinary procedure. A gap in PIB-named awards between the two firms is what entry dates and capability predict. PIB also does not publish emergency procurements (for example Drishti-10 UAVs), below-threshold orders or MRO awards (Air Works), so Adani-linked receipts may be understated. L&T's may be too.",
