        "denialFound": "None found; not asked. None is needed: this is a descriptive split that accuses no one. The MoD's own counter-figure is the 81% domestic / 19% non-domestic value split for FY2024-25 in PRID 2116411, which should appear beside the sample.",
        "innocentReading": "This matches the record's own innocentReading. A few mega-contracts go to the only domestic designer of each platform: LCA 2021 and 2025, LCH 2025, AL-31FP engines 2024, Su-30 2024. PIB releases leave out most foreign G2G/FMS deals or print no ₹ figure for them (Rafale-M IGA PRID 2124851 has no ₹; MQ-9B value not stated). DPSU primes pass much of the value on to private sub-suppliers. So a PIB-sampled split will over-state DPSU share and under-state foreign share, and that says nothing about how vendors are treated.",
        "reason": "The arithmetic reproduces exactly, and the three cited PIB releases confirm the HAL amounts (₹48,000 crore, ₹62,700 crore and ₹62,370 crore). The claim still fails as written, for two reasons. (1) The label \"PIB-named MoD awards 2021-25\" describes a set that is exhaustive by definition, but the tally is a hand-picked subset. It leaves out a PIB-named foreign award with a printed ₹ figure that sits in a source the record itself cites: PRID 2209832, \"48 Heavy Weight Torpedoes ... at an approximate cost of Rs 1,896 crore was signed with WASS Submarine Systems S.R.L.\" The file even lists it as a documented foreign contract. It also leaves out other PIB-named, priced awards (Naval Group ₹877 crore, MDL ₹1,990 crore, BEL Ashwini ₹2,906 crore, HVF Arjun ₹7,523 crore). (2) The headline \"foreign 5.4%\" sits beside a cited MoD universe figure (PRID 2116411: domestic 81% of ₹2,09,050 crore in FY2024-25) showing the sample under-represents foreign value by a factor of about 3-4 in the years it covers. The \"sample, not universe\" caveat says that coverage is partial. It does not say the sample is biased, or which direction the bias runs. The analytic finding that DPSUs dominate PIB-named value holds up, so this needs correcting, not killing.",
