        "denialFound": "Not applicable. This is our own analytic comparison and accuses no party. No party was asked. None found.",
        "innocentReading": "The shares move with the Sixth Pay Commission (arrears in 2008-10), OROP and the Seventh Pay Commission (2016-17), not with which party is in office. UPA-II's nominal growth looks high because inflation was high. NDA's last endpoint is lifted by a new Rs 37,200 cr of spectrum-charges lines in BE 2026-27 (D20 items 6.04/7.05/8.04). Without them the NDA nominal CAGR is about 8.4%. The real CAGR uses BE 2025-26, which has no spectrum lines, so it is unaffected. The windows are unequal: 4 growth intervals against 12. The record prints the NDA first-five-years figures (9.1% nominal / 5.6% real) as a like-for-like check. The 2016-17 restructuring of the demands moves money between revenue and civil but leaves the four-demand total unchanged.",
