        "innocentReading": "Delhi Police is the capital's police under Article 239AA, and the Union pays for it whoever governs Delhi. Its multi-year growth matches the Police demand under both governments. The FY2021-22 step is not opaque at head level. MHA's Detailed Demands put most of it in one object head, 2055.00.119.01.01.28 'Professional Services', which was 172.20 cr actual in FY2020-21 against a BE of 252.00 cr. It then reached 2,132.05 cr at RE 2021-22 and 2,152.16 cr actual 2021-22, then 1,572.00 cr at RE 2022-23. That accounts for about 1,980 cr (64%) of the 3,116 cr step. Salaries add about 534 cr (6,179.93 to 6,713.98). Boring fits that remain open: outsourced or contract services (manpower, CCTV/communications O&M, IT), a reclassification of payments previously booked elsewhere, or settlement of dues. The Detailed Demands name the head but not the purpose.",
