        "innocentReading": "The fall is mostly the denominator. Pay commissions, DA and new battalions inflate revenue while capital in the force lines stays at a few hundred crore per force. The force lines also hold only a narrow slice of CAPF capital, and that is true in both periods, not just under NDA. In 2011-12 actuals, CPO housing (item 29.01, 607.15 cr) and CPO buildings (item 30.01, 1,760.17 cr) sat in separate lines, as did Border Management capital (992.46 cr) and the aircraft/boats 'Misc. Items' line. In 2024-25, 'Building Projects of CAPFs and CPOs' was 1,894.58 cr, Border Infrastructure capital outlay 3,649.79 cr, BSF Air Wing 72.52 cr and Modernization Plan IV 119.24 cr. All of these lie outside the seven lines. Which way the ratio moves depends on which lines are counted: adding border infrastructure (BOPs and fencing, largely CAPF-used) probably raises the NDA figure, while adding CPO buildings probably lowers it.",
        "reason": "The claim survives Lens A. The arithmetic reproduces exactly from the file's budget rows: UPA-II capital 3,048.04 of 116,729.12 crore and NDA 12,996.79 of 780,080.29 crore, giving 2.61% and 1.67%, with ratios of 37:1 and 59:1. I checked the rows against the primary PDFs I opened. The 2013-14 Demand 55 shows 2011-12 4055 actuals CRPF 325.09, NSG 36.51, BSF 263.47, ITBP 85.31, CISF 22.00, AR 96.60, SSB 55.57, which sum to 884.55. The 2026-27 Demand 51 shows 2024-25 capital CRPF 545.52, NSG 27.89, BSF 664.96, ITBP 133.31, CISF 54.03, AR 356.88, SSB 180.70. The 2016-17 Demand 48 shows CRPF 2014-15 4055 at 226.63. The 2026-27 scheme figures quoted in the innocentReading are also correct: Building Projects 5,040.87 and MP-IV 343.66 at BE 2026-27. The claim is analytic, implies no wrongdoing, and carries an innocentReading, so 'analytic' is the right tier. Lens B does not kill it, but it is misleading by how the periods are split. The series shows a decline that begins inside UPA-II (3.30% to 1.85% by FY2013-14), not a break in 2014. The innocentReading also does not say that the building and border lines were separate in both periods, or that border infrastructure capital, used largely by CAPFs, grew sharply under NDA. sourceCheck is 'partially' because the claim cites only 4 of the roughly 15 Expenditure Budget files its 15 years of actuals come from. The 2013-14 file supplies only 2011-12 actuals, and the 2018-19 file supplies only 2016-17.",
