        "denialFound": "No denial addressed to the 'handed to builders' allegation was found, and I found no record that MoD was asked about it. MoD's stated reason, PIB 1942023 (24 Jul 2023): \"In order to bring uniformity in municipal laws governing civil areas of Cantonments and adjoining State Municipal areas, it has been decided to consider to excise civil areas of certain Cantonments and merge them with neighbouring State municipalities.\" https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=1942023",
        "innocentReading": "This is municipal normalisation, not a sale. Civil areas of colonial-era cantonments go to state municipalities so residents can use state welfare schemes and MoD stops paying for civic upkeep. Military areas become 'exclusive military stations' under Army control. For Khasyol, the Tribune (2023) reports that \"the military area within the cantonment will be converted into a military station and the civil area will be merged with the municipality\" (Dharamshala MC). Under the third modified proposal (Deccan Chronicle, 9 Aug 2024), proprietary rights over civic assets go to states and municipalities \"at no cost\", and \"ownership of vacant land parcels will remain with the MoD\". In this reading the transferee is the state or municipality, not a private builder. The one opening for the narrative is in the same report: if transferred land is sold or leased, 50 per cent of the income goes to a share. That is a monetisation clause, not a record of any transfer to a builder.",
        "reason": "The three cited sources do say 62, 62 and 61, so the numbers are right. The framing is refuted. 'One documented drop in thirteen years, no land-transfer record opened' leaves out a primary PIB record (PRID 1942023, 24 Jul 2023). That record confirms the abolition half of the narrative as stated policy: civil areas of 58 cantonments are to be excised, and Khasyol was de-notified w.e.f. 27.04.2023. A March 2024 MoD notification (Tribune, 8 Mar 2024) then listed areas in 10 cantonments for excision. So 'cantonments are being abolished' is documented in substance: cantonment status is being dissolved, the civil areas are merged and the military areas are kept as military stations. Only the motive clause ('so defence land can be handed to builders') lacks support. The available records name states and municipalities as transferees and say MoD keeps vacant land. The record's own falsifier ('a record that Khasyol's land remains with the Army as a military station') is already met by public reporting, and the record did not look. Calling the whole narrative 'speculative' on 'one drop' understates the premise and overstates our ignorance of the mechanism. The narrative should be split: the excision programme as documented (PIB 1942023), and the builders motive as unsupported or speculative. The assessment itself is our own analysis, so it should carry an innocentReading.",
