        "sourceCheck": "source-does-not-say",
        "denialFound": "Yes, several. (a) Parrikar's file noting of 2016-01-11, read out by Defence Minister Sitharaman in Parliament on 2019-02-08: \"It appears that PMO and French President's office are monitoring the progress of the issues which was an outcome of the summit meeting. Para 5 appears to be an over reaction\"; Sitharaman called The Hindu's cropped publication unethical (Swarajya, HT, Free Press Journal reports, via https://swarajyamag.com/politics/rafale-story-of-the-day-was-parrikars-name-and-reply-cropped-out-on-purpose). (b) Air Marshal S.B.P. Sinha, head of the Indian Negotiating Team, 2019-02-08: \"No such objections were ever brought to me by anybody from the Ministry of Defence. I am hearing about the letter for the first time.\" (https://theprint.in/defence/nobody-flagged-any-objections-before-me-says-iaf-officer-who-led-rafale-negotiations/189634/). (c) Former Defence Secretary G. Mohan Kumar said the note \"had nothing to do with price\", and was about the sovereign guarantee and general terms. (d) Deccan Herald headline \"PMO did not engage in parallel negotiation in Rafale\" (https://www.deccanherald.com/amp/story/india%2Fpmo-did-not-engage-in-parallel-negotiation-in-rafale-732115.html, returned 403 and was not opened). The SC review judgment of 2019-11-14 (https://indiankanoon.org/doc/26499003/) records the parallel-negotiations point only as the petitioners' case (\"documents which suggest that there were parallel negotiations being undertaken by the Prime Minister's Office (PMO) which was strenuously objected to by the Indian Negotiating Team\") and dismissed the review: \"All aspects were considered by the competent authority and the different views expressed considered\".",
        "innocentReading": "This was a summit-originated government-to-government deal. The PMO, and the French President's office on the other side, followed up on unresolved issues: sovereign guarantee, bank guarantee and general terms. Desk officials saw this as cutting across their formal negotiating channel and protested. The minister ruled that it was monitoring, not negotiation, and told the Defence Secretary to settle it with the Principal Secretary to the PM. The formal team (INT) kept negotiating, and the deal went through the DAC and CCS. This reading fits every document in hand as well as \"parallel negotiations over MoD's objection\" does.",
        "reason": "Neither cited source says what the claim says. The SC order of 2019-04-10 (indiankanoon doc 126750916) is purely about admissibility. It never mentions \"parallel\", \"PMO\" or \"negotiat\"; it only holds that the three documents were published and their contents were not disputed. The current Wikipedia article on the Rafale deal controversy has no mention of The Hindu documents, the PMO or parallel negotiations. The record admits The Hindu's articles were never opened. On substance, the documented fact is narrower: MoD officials objected to \"parallel parleys\" by the PMO. The claim's wording, \"the PMO ran parallel negotiations over MoD's objection\", takes the officials' description as fact and treats the officials as \"MoD\". But the Defence Minister wrote on the file that it was \"monitoring\" and called the objection an \"over reaction\". The head of the negotiating team said no objection ever reached him. The SC review judgment records the point only as the petitioners' allegation and dismissed the review. Calling a contested description from one side of an internal dispute \"well-supported\" overstates the evidence. It belongs at alleged with a contra. Its documented core, that the note existed and its authenticity was not contested, can be carried as reported.",
        "corrections": [
          "1. Reword the claim: \"MoD officials, in a note of 2015-11-24 published by The Hindu in Feb 2019, objected to 'parallel parleys' by the PMO with French officials; the then Defence Minister minuted on 2016-01-11 that the PMO was 'monitoring the progress' and the objection was 'an over reaction'.\" 2. Change status from \"well-supported\" to \"contested\", and set the tier to alleged for \"PMO ran parallel negotiations\". Keep \"the note exists and its authenticity was not disputed\" at reported/documented. 3. Fix srcs. Drop Wikipedia as support: it does not say this. Keep the 2019-04-10 SC order only for admissibility. Add the SC review judgment https://indiankanoon.org/doc/26499003/ (records the claim as the petitioners' case and dismisses the review), and add The Hindu 2019-02-08 article (N. Ram), or ThePrint/HT coverage, as the actual source for the note. 4. Add contra entries: Parrikar's file noting (via Sitharaman, Lok Sabha 2019-02-08); INT head Air Marshal S.B.P. Sinha (ThePrint 2019-02-08); G. Mohan Kumar (\"nothing to do with price\"). 5. In strongestCounter, change \"the Defence Minister of the day overruled the objection\" to quote his words (\"monitoring\", \"over reaction\"). 6. Do not name the Deputy Secretary who signed the note (below public rank). 7. whatWouldChangeThis: \"Up\" needs the PMO's own records of the meetings with French officials, or a CAG/court finding, not just the MoD file."
        ],
