        "denialFound": "MoD has not denied the claim directly. Its official position is promotional: PIB 2273824 credits \"increased private sector participation\". Other sources argue both ways, and the narrative should cite them. Supporting the protection reading: the CVC April 2021 memo said \"award of contracts/projects/procurements on nomination basis without adequate justification amounts to restrictive practice eliminating competition\", and private-industry complaints are documented (Defense News 2022-08-08, https://www.defensenews.com/top-100/2022/08/08/indias-private-defense-firms-seek-level-playing-field-as-mod-preps-new-arms-embargo/; Bharat Shakti, https://bharatshakti.in/defence-procurement-not-a-level-playing-field-for-private-sector-pses-still-rule/). Against it: ThePrint 2026-05-27 reports that in the AMCA prototype tender \"State-run Hindustan Aeronautics Limited (HAL) has been kept out of the bidding process\", with TASL, a Bharat Forge consortium and an L&T consortium shortlisted (https://theprint.in/defence/5th-gen-fighter-amca-tender-issued-hal-sits-out-as-private-sector-takes-centre-stage/2943139/). HAL and the DPSUs were not asked for comment.",
        "innocentReading": "DPSUs win most award value because they are the sole design or licence holders for the platforms being bought: HAL for LCA, LCH, ALH and Su-30/AL-31FP under Russian licence, and BDL for DRDO's Akash. Repeat orders go to the incumbent producer whatever its ownership, as the L&T K9 repeat order shows. DPSU primes also pass much of their contract value to private suppliers (about 60% on Akash). Where a new category opened (towed guns, high-power radar, CIWS, carbines, AMCA prototypes), private firms have won or been the only ones shortlisted.",
        "reason": "The narrative survives, but only as a contested analytic synthesis. Every quoted fact I opened is confirmed by the primary record: the PIB releases for ATAGS, K9, HPR/CIWS, CQB and Akash's 60%, PIB 2273824's 76%/24%/22%, and the MoD AR 2024-25 production table. The 58% recomputes exactly from the file's award claims. The status \"contested\" is the correct reading, and an adversarial reading cannot push it to \"true\" or \"false\".\n\nThree faults remain, and none is fatal. (1) \"~74-76% of production\" joins a DPSU+ex-OFB figure to a DPSU+other-PSU figure. (2) None of the four cited sources states the 77%/58%; those are our own computation on a hand-picked sample, and \"PIB-named award ₹\" reads as the universe. (3) The strongest case leaves out the actual documented mechanism of protection (nomination-basis awards, the 2021 CVC memo). The strongest counter leaves out the reported 2026 AMCA tender that excluded HAL, which is inside the asOf window. \"narrative\" is not a valid tier; the closest valid tier is analytic.",
